  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "CB08320",
    "sub_id": "41135",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": null,
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": "Classroom behavior should always be timely, professional, well-prepared, and polite. Students, instructors, and guest speakers should maintain mutual dignity and respect to facilitate effective learning.\n1. Students should attend classes punctually. If you cannot arrive on time, please do not enroll in the course. Unless you are ill or have an emergency, you should be present in the classroom and seated before the class begins. If you need to leave early, please inform the instructor in advance.\n2. All students should respect everyone in the classroom and conduct themselves in a reasonable, responsible, and polite manner at all times.\n3. Avoid talking, reading, sleeping, or working on unrelated tasks during class, except when engaged in group discussions. Minimize side conversations.\n4. Laptops, tablets, and other devices may be used for note-taking, but should be put away otherwise.\n5. Turn off and put away mobile phones, PDAs, and other devices, keeping them silent during class.\n6. Wearing headphones during class is not permitted.",
    "course_pol_en": null,
    "course_rem": "Requirement: If you have never taken classes related to \"economic quantitative analysis,\" please do not select this course.\n\nAll students are expected to adhere to the following communication guidelines:\n1. Teaching and learning communication between teachers and students should utilize the o365 email as the common tool.\n2. When communicating via email, announcements, or other means with teachers and classmates, ensure information is clear and maintain politeness.\n3. Emails should be signed; anonymous emails will not receive a response.\n4. For inquiries regarding course-related questions, please email during weekdays from Monday to Friday.",
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<ol>\n\t<li>Integrity is the foundation of learning. Any student who attempts to submit notes copied in a dishonest manner, which they did not take during the course, is engaging in dishonest behavior.</li>\n\t<li>For students caught cheating, plagiarizing, or aiding others in assignments, tests, or exams, the grade for that instance will be zero. Repeat offenders will be referred according to Feng Chia University&#39;s student disciplinary regulations.</li>\n\t<li>All assessments, including course materials, notes, and exams, where copying answers or submitting work that is not one&#39;s own is detected, are considered acts of dishonesty. Penalties outlined in the course regulations will be enforced, and severe cases may result in disciplinary action according to Feng Chia University&#39;s student disciplinary regulations.</li>\n</ol>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": null,
    "ilearn_mk": null
  },
